.TH LOGX 1 "July 2026" "logx 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
logx \- query nginx logs in plain English
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logx
.BI \-q " QUERY"
.RB [ \-src
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-dsl | \-\-cmd ]
.RB [ \-x ]
.RB [ \-Q ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.IB "producer " |
.B logx
.BI \-q " QUERY"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B logx
translates a natural-language question into a small, schema-validated JSON
DSL using a local 15M-parameter seq2seq model (no network, no data egress),
then compiles that DSL into a read-only
.BR awk (1)
pipeline and runs it over an nginx access or error log.
.PP
The result rows are written to
.IR stdout .
The DSL translation is echoed to
.I stderr
(one line, prefixed
.BR "logx:" )
so you can always see how your question was understood without polluting
piped output. Suppress it with
.BR \-Q .
.PP
Input is chosen in this order: an explicit
.BI \-src " FILE"
(gzip-compressed
.B .gz
files are handled transparently); piped
.I stdin
when no file is given (e.g.
.BR "tail \-n 5000 access.log | logx ..." );
otherwise the standard nginx locations
.I /var/log/nginx/access.log
and
.IR /var/log/nginx/error.log .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-q ", " \-\-query " QUERY"
The question to ask. May also be given as a bare positional argument.
.TP
.BI \-src ", " \-\-src " FILE"
Log file to query.
.B \-
means stdin explicitly.
.TP
.B \-\-dsl
Print the canonical DSL JSON to stdout and exit without executing.
Useful for scripting and for auditing the translation.
.TP
.B \-\-cmd
Print the equivalent shell pipeline to stdout and exit without executing.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-explain
Additionally print the model confidence and the compiled pipeline to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the DSL echo on stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-conf\-threshold " N"
Mean token-logprob gate. Translations scoring below
.I N
are refused (exit 2). Default \-1.0 (loose).
.TP
.BI \-\-model\-dir " DIR"
Use a different trained model directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Pipeline timeout in file mode (default 30). Stream mode has no timeout.
.TP
.B \-\-manual
Open this manual.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-\-help
.SH SUPPORTED QUERIES
Four actions over nginx access and error logs:
.BR show / filter
(print matching lines),
.B count
(optionally grouped by a field), and
.B top
(top-K values of a field). Filters support eq/ne/gte/lte/contains/regex on
fields such as ip, status, path, method, bytes, referer, user-agent (access)
and level, pid, client, message (error). Time windows: relative
.RB ( "last 15 minutes/hours/days" )
or absolute ISO ranges. Questions outside this scope make the model emit
.B abstain
and logx exits with status 2 rather than guessing.
.SH EXAMPLES
Top talkers in a rotated log:
.PP
.nf
.RS
logx \-q "top 5 ips" \-src /var/log/nginx/access.log.2.gz
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compose with standard tools \(em only the last hour of a busy log:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tail \-n 100000 access.log | logx \-q "how many 502s"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Watch matching lines live (show/filter only \(em see LIMITATIONS):
.PP
.nf
.RS
tail \-f access.log | logx \-q "show POST requests with status 500"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Audit before you trust \(em print the DSL or the pipeline instead of running:
.PP
.nf
.RS
logx \-\-dsl \-q "count 404s in the last 2 hours"
logx \-\-cmd \-q "top 10 paths by requests" \-src access.log
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage or environment error (bad flags, missing file, missing model).
.TP
.B 2
Abstain: the question is out of scope, or confidence fell below the gate.
Nothing was executed.
.TP
.B 3
The model produced invalid DSL (rare, ~2%). Nothing was executed.
.TP
.B 4
The pipeline itself failed (I/O error, timeout).
.SH SAFETY
Defense in depth; every layer must pass before anything runs:
.IP \(bu 3
The DSL is canonicalized and schema-validated first; low-confidence and
.B abstain
translations stop with exit 2.
.IP \(bu 3
Execution never touches a shell. The pipeline is a chain of argv vectors
restricted to an allowlist of read-only binaries (awk, sort, zcat, ...).
.IP \(bu 3
Filter values never enter awk program text \(em they are passed as
.B awk \-v
variables, so log contents and query values cannot inject code.
.IP \(bu 3
The model runs fully offline; log data never leaves the machine.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOGX_HOME
Install root (set by the launcher; override to relocate).
.TP
.B LOGX_MODEL_DIR
Model directory override, same as
.BR \-\-model\-dir .
.TP
.B LOGX_CONF_THRESHOLD
Default for
.BR \-\-conf\-threshold .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/lib/logx/
Default install root: model weights, schema, code, private venv.
.TP
.I /var/log/nginx/{access,error}.log
Default query targets when no \-src is given and stdin is a terminal.
.SH LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 3
nginx combined access-log and standard error-log formats only.
.IP \(bu 3
.B count
and
.B top
aggregate at end-of-input, so they need finite input \(em they will not
produce output under
.BR "tail \-f" .
Live streaming works for show/filter, best when logx writes directly to a
terminal.
.IP \(bu 3
Time filters compare wall-clock timestamps; timezone offsets are ignored.
.IP \(bu 3
The translation is a model prediction (~90% exact-match). For anything that
matters, glance at the echoed DSL or use
.BR \-\-dsl / \-\-cmd
first.
.IP \(bu 3
Each invocation loads the model (a few seconds). A resident daemon mode is
planned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR awk (1),
.BR tail (1),
.BR grep (1)
